Subject: [PATCH 04853/11362] [outer-loop] Conductor gate-config fixes:
 un-quarantine the 4 tests (fix #1 already resolved via --no-cov)

Operator-directed (after the n=200 result + conductor at the .458->.459 boundary). Addressing the two
gate-config fixes:

FIX #1 (transition gate slowness) -- ALREADY RESOLVED in-repo, verified: the latest transition module
exp4968 uses `pytest <own-test> -q --no-cov` and the conductor's own full-suite gate already uses
`--no-cov -o addopts=` (research_conductor.py:1354). No transition cap-fail since 12:48 UTC. Documented the
DURABILITY REQUIREMENT in ops/known-issues.md so future transition modules keep --no-cov + own-test.

FIX #2 (the 4 quarantined tests) -- ROOT CAUSE was NOT real-I/O hangs: diagnosed that 4940/4941/4943/4944
are heavy-compute tests made ~15x slower by COVERAGE instrumentation (6s each with --no-cov vs 90s+ with
coverage); the full coverage-instrumented suite then blew the codex cap. With coverage off in every
conductor gate (fix #1), they pass in ~6s and no longer threaten a cap -> UN-QUARANTINED (removed from
conftest collect_ignore). Verified: all 4 collected + 47 passed in 2.99s with --no-cov. No mocking needed
(they were never broken). Restores their coverage in CI/full-suite runs (which have no codex cap).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
